title: Repository layout on disk
tags: Daemon
kind: reference
summary: What .metafolder/ holds — config.json and its fields, schema.json, and the internal/ directory nothing tracks.

```
.metafolder/
  config.json          the repository's identity and settings
  schema.json          the optional user schema
  gui/history/<zone>   the GUI's input histories (written by the GUI)
  internal/            never tracked
    kv/                the key-value store (LMDB data.mdb, daemon.lock)
    trash/             the trash-bin (blobs and their index)
    slow/              the slow-operation log
    backups/           the backups (auto/, manual-<time>/)
    …                  the per-pair sync databases, the case probe
```

`internal/` is excluded from tracking by absolute path, in the watcher and in
reconcile alike; everything else in `.metafolder/` is trackable content. The
store ([[Storage]]) is refused on a network filesystem ([[Storage safety]]). `internal/kv/daemon.lock` is held with
`flock` for as long as a daemon has the repository loaded.

!! config.json

|!Field |!Type |!Meaning |
|`repo_uuid` |uuid |the repository's stable identifier |
|`name` |string |its name, unique among loaded repositories (renamed with `PATCH /repos/:repo`) |
|`version` |integer |the version of this file's layout |
|`root` |path |the watched directory, absolute — usually `.metafolder/`'s parent, anywhere for an external one |
|`schema` |path |optional: the user schema, relative to `.metafolder/` or absolute (default `.metafolder/schema.json`) |
|`created_at` |integer |creation time, Unix seconds |
|`log_retention_revisions` |integer |optional: how many revisions of history the log keeps, overriding the daemon's setting (`0`: everything) ([[Automatic retention]]) |
|`log_retention_keep_labels` |bool |optional: whether a labelled revision stops the trim, overriding the daemon's setting |
|`system` |bool |a repository the daemon uses internally (a sync plan repository): hidden from `GET /repos` unless `?all=true` |
|`storage` |string |the store holding the data: the key-value store. Absent means a SQLite repository from before September 2026, which is refused at load ([[How the storage backend was built]]) |

It is JSON, not TOML, because it is written by the daemon, not by you: it is
repository data, distinct from the daemon's own `config.toml`
([[Daemon configuration]]).
